  "rating": {
    "inherent": "critical",
    "residual": "high",
    "forecast": "critical",
    "rationale": "Inherent risk is critical because an untrusted inbound email can drive a broad CRM lookup (any customer, by a token that can read every record) followed by an unreviewed send through a shared service account that can mail any address (finding.lethal_trifecta), a classic lethal trifecta. The only credited control today is a behavioral prompt instruction against cross-customer sharing, which brings residual to high but no lower, since no structural control severs or narrows the path (no recipient binding, no credential scoping, no approval gate). Two further present weaknesses hold residual at high: unauthenticated, unpinned MCP connections carrying broadly scoped shared tokens (finding.mcp_trust_gaps), and the absence of any rate, spend, or step limit on reads or sends (finding.no_volume_limits). A missing audit trail for CRM reads (finding.crm_read_audit_gap) is low because the affected capability is read-only. Forecast returns to critical because the one preventive control is dependent on model compliance and the model is upgraded with the platform with no separate review (subject.model.swappable = true), so a model upgrade, a longer task horizon, or an autonomy increase would strip the agent's only present mitigation and reopen the full inherent path."
  },
  "limitations": [
    "This assessment reflects the declared design and configuration in prompt.md, mcp.json, and the runtime notes; it does not reflect observed runtime behavior of the deployed agent.",
